<!DOCTYPE Bill PUBLIC "-//LSC//DTD Authoring Bill XML//EN" "l:\dtd\author\billauthoring.top"><Bill version="1.0" type="introLN" docName="H-1949.1"><IntroducedBillHeader><RequestNumber>H-1949.1</RequestNumber><BillNumber>HOUSE BILL 2165</BillNumber><StateLegSession><State>State of Washington</State><Legislature>58th Legislature</Legislature><Session>2003 Regular Session</Session></StateLegSession><Sponsors>Representatives Conway and Wood</Sponsors><IntroHistory><ReadDate>Read first time 02/28/2003.  </ReadDate><ReferredTo>Referred to Committee on Commerce &amp; Labor.</ReferredTo></IntroHistory></IntroducedBillHeader><BriefDescription>Concerning the appliance repair specialty.</BriefDescription><BillBody><PullFooter logNumber="H-1949.1/03" attorneyInitials="ML" typistInitials="mos" dateCreated="02/22/2003"/><BillTitle><LineNumber line=" 1" page="1,1" hrt="no"/>	AN ACT Relating to electrical licensing and certification<LineNumber line=" 2" page="1,2"/>requirements applicable to persons working in the appliance repair<LineNumber line=" 3" page="1,3"/>specialty; and creating a new section.</BillTitle><EnactingClause><LineNumber line=" 4" page="1,4" hrt="no"/>BE IT ENACTED BY THE LEGISLATURE OF THE STATE OF WASHINGTON:</EnactingClause><BillSection type="new"><LineNumber line=" 5" page="1,5" hrt="no"/><BegSecNew><NewSecText>NEW SECTION.</NewSecText><SecNum>Sec. </SecNum></BegSecNew><RCWSLText>The legislature finds that, under current<LineNumber line=" 6" page="1,6"/>law, persons who work in the appliance repair specialty are subject to<LineNumber line=" 7" page="1,7"/>electrical licensing and certification requirements.</RCWSLText></BillSection><BillEnd>--- END ---<PageNumberFooter lastpage="yes">		p. 1	HB 2165</PageNumberFooter></BillEnd></BillBody></Bill>